1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bc4 e6 7. O-O a6 8. Bb3
Be7 9. f4 O-O 10. Be3 Bd7 11. Qf3 Qc7 12. f5 Nxd4 13. Bxd4 e5 14. Be3 b5 $146
15. g4 $11 (15. Rac1 Bc6 $14) 15... b4 16. Nd5 Nxd5 17. Bxd5 (17. exd5 $6 a5
18. Qe4 Rfc8 $15) 17... Bc6 18. Bxc6 Qxc6 19. g5 f6 20. g6 h6 $14 {
Consolidates g5} (20... Rfd8 21. Rad1 $11) 21. Rad1 $11 (21. Rfc1 Rad8 22. c4
Rc8 $16) 21... Rfd8 22. Rf2 Bf8 23. Rg2 Rd7 24. Kh1 Rad8 25. Rd5 {The white
rook on an outpost} Qc4 26. b3 Qc3 27. Qe2 Rc8 {Attacks the backward pawn on c2
} 28. Bc1 Rdc7 {Increases the pressure on the backward pawn} 29. Qd1 Rc5 30.
Rd3 $11 (30. a3 Rxd5 31. Qxd5+ Kh8 32. axb4 Qe1+ 33. Rg1 Qe2 34. Bxh6 Qf3+ 35.
Rg2 Qf1+ 36. Rg1 Qf3+ 37. Rg2 Qf1+ 38. Rg1 Qf3+ $11) 30... Qa1 31. c4 bxc3 32.
Qc2 {White threatens Rd1} d5 33. exd5 $11 (33. Rd1 $142 $5 dxe4 34. b4 $16)
33... Rd8 34. Rg1 {Threatening Ba3} Ra5 $18 (34... Rcxd5 35. Rxd5 $1 {a
convincing end} Rxd5 $18) 35. a4 $16 (35. Ba3 $1 Qxg1+ 36. Kxg1 Bxa3 37. Qxc3
$18) 35... Raxd5 $2 $18 (35... Bc5 $142 36. Rgd1 Bd4 $16) 36. Rxd5 $1 {a
fitting end to a beautiful game. Threatening mate: Rxd8} (36. Qxc3 {is clearly
weaker} Qb1 37. Rxd5 Qe4+ 38. Rg2 Rxd5 $17) (36. Rxc3 $6 Rd1 $11) 36... Rxd5
37. Qe4 $4 $14 {White loses the upper hand} (37. b4 $142 $18) 37... Rd8 $2 $18
(37... Rd4 $142 {is the best option Black has} 38. Qb7 Rd8 $14) 38. Bxh6 (38.
Qc4+ Kh8 39. Bxh6 Qa3 $18) 38... Rd1 $4 {the position was bad, and this
mistake simply hastens the end} (38... Rd4 39. Qxd4 $1 {White goes into the
lead} exd4 40. Rxa1 gxh6 $19) 39. Qc4+ {And mate in four. This won the
brilliancy prize at Coventry.} (39. Qc4+ Rd5 40. Qxd5+ Kh8 41. Bxg7+ Kxg7 42.
Qf7+ Kh8 43. Qxf8#) 1-0

