1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 c5 4. d5 exd5 5. cxd5 g6 6. Nf3 d6 7. g3 Bg7 8. Bg2
O-O 9. O-O a6 10. a4 Nbd7 11. Nd2 Rb8 12. Nc4 Nb6 13. Qd3 $11 (13. Nxd6 $142 $5
Bg4 14. a5 $16) 13... Bf5 14. e4 Nxc4 15. Qxc4 b5 16. axb5 axb5 17. Nxb5 {
Black gets strong play along the open e-file} Bxe4 18. Bf4 $17 (18. Bxe4 $142
$5 {must definitely be considered} Nxe4 19. f3 $11) 18... Bxg2 19. Kxg2 Nxd5
20. Qxd5 {d6 seems the pivot of the position} Rxb5 21. Rad1 $17 (21. Ra6 $5 $15
) 21... Rxb2 22. Be3 $19 (22. Bxd6 $5 Bd4 23. Rb1 $15) 22... Re8 23. Kg1 Bf8
24. Bf4 Rb4 25. Rd2 Qf6 26. Rfd1 Rbe4 27. Bxd6 Qf3 {The mate threat is Re1} 28.
Rf1 Bxd6 29. Qxd6 Re1 {Threatening mate... how?} 30. Qd3 Rxf1+ 31. Qxf1 c4 32.
Qd1 c3 33. Rd8 (33. Qxf3 $4 {going for material but overlooking...} Re1+ 34.
Kg2 cxd2 $19) 33... Qxd1+ 34. Rxd1 c2 $15 (34... Rc8 $5 $17) 35. Rc1 Rc8 36.
Kf1 Kg7 37. Ke2 Kf6 38. Kd3 Kf5 39. f3 g5 40. h3 h5 (40... h5 41. Kd2 h4 42.
gxh4 gxh4 $19) 0-1

